{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And He said: Behold, I cut a covenant.</b> And this is, for according to these words I have cut a covenant with you (Exodus 34:27), and they are the conditions written from the beginning of 'Observe for yourself' (Exodus 34:11), and on account of this I will write for you the second tablets, and it shall be like a deed of testimony, and all this, that I forgave their iniquity, was for your sake; therefore I will do wonders with you, so that all who see you shall marvel, and they shall know that I have placed splendor upon you, which I have not done since the day I created heaven and earth. And this is the matter of the shining of His face, and behold it is written of him at his death: 'And his eye was not dim, nor his moisture departed' (Deuteronomy 34:7) — the opposite of the nature of all old men." "<b>And the meaning of 'which were not created in all the earth.'</b> This was not heard among the nations. And the Gaon [Saadia] said: 'which were not created thus in all the land of Egypt, from which you came forth, and among all the nations.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "Resolved הגאון not present here; epithet resolution not needed for this comment. The phrase דבר קרינות פניו (lit. 'the matter of the shining of His face') reads literally; the construction is unusual but the sense follows the context of Moses' shining face."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:16.359993976Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}